Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:31:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 082/119] scene-referred S4: the stock LDR stage goes inert
 (D9)

With the scene-referred pipeline running, everything the stock engine does AFTER the display
transform is grading a picture that has already been squeezed onto a monitor. It can only
redistribute code values that survived the transform, which is exactly the "JPEG feel" this
pipeline exists to get away from. D9 skips the whole stage; after the ODT only dither remains.

Skipped at the STAGE level rather than by driving parameters to neutral - a neutral pass still
costs a full-screen read and a write, and a nulled parameter is a silent lie to anyone reading
the value back:

- CPostEffectStage::Execute() does not preprocess Sharpening, Blurring or UberGamePostProcess
  (vignette, saturation, artefacts).
- CPostAAStage::DoFinalComposition() drops the film grain, the sharpening flag and the flare
  colour-chart re-grade. The pass itself is not skippable - with the post-effect stage active it
  is the only path from the display target to the back buffer - so what is gated is the work
  inside it.
- The tone map already does not set the colour chart flag (previous commit).

CColorGradingStage keeps running: it is cached and cheap, and leaving it alive means turning the
camera off restores the stock look immediately instead of after a chart rebuild.

What still runs: PostAA and SMAA, the final blit, dither, EFSLIST_AFTER_HDRPOSTPROCESS, the HUD,
and all of ours - the viewfinder overlays, the lens-optics composite, the squeeze/letterbox remap
and the lateral chromatic aberration. None of our effects sits after the ODT, so nothing had to
move; the one that composites late (lens optics) is display-referred by construction and is
listed as breakage for S7 rather than moved here.

One line in the log per flip of the switch says which stock effects have gone inert, because a
user reaching for a slider that does nothing deserves an explanation in the log rather than a
mystery.

